/A 2096 0 R
/Alt (The four panel raincloud plot arranged two by two compares alpha diversity metrics between IBD and No IBD groups. Each panel displays half violin plots, box plots, and jittered individual points. Panel A, labelled Kruskal Wallis p equals 0.420, shows Observed ASVs on the vertical axis. The IBD group has a median around 60, while the No IBD group has a median around 70. Panel B, labelled Kruskal Wallis p equals 0.045, shows Shannon diversity on the vertical axis. The IBD group has a median around 2.2, while the No IBD group has a median around 2.8, with a significant difference indicated by an asterisk. Panel C, labelled Kruskal Wallis p equals 0.093, shows Pielou evenness on the vertical axis. Both groups have medians around 0.6. Panel D, labelled Kruskal Wallis p equals 0.121, shows Simpson diversity on the vertical axis. Both groups have medians around 0.8.)
