/A 2099 0 R
/Alt (The two panel graph arranged side by side shows principal coordinate analysis. Panel a, on the left, displays a scatter plot of Bray Curtis distance PCoA2 on the vertical axis, ranging from 0.0 to 0.8, versus Bray Curtis distance PCoA1 on the horizontal axis, ranging from minus 0.4 to 0.4. A density plot above the horizontal axis shows two overlapping distributions, one peaking near 0.0 and another slightly to the right. A density plot to the right of the vertical axis shows two overlapping distributions, one peaking near 0.0 and another slightly above 0.0. The plot contains two groups: IBD and No IBD. IBD points are represented by circular markers and No IBD points by circular markers. The p PER&#132;M&#132;A&#132;N&#132;OVA value is 0.595. Panel b, on the right, displays a scatter plot of Jaccard distance PCoA2 on the vertical axis, ranging from minus 0.2 to 0.4, versus Jaccard distance PCoA1 on the horizontal axis, ranging from minus 0.2 to 0.4. A density plot above the horizontal axis shows two overlapping distributions, one peaking near 0.0 and another slightly to the right. A density plot to the right of the vertical axis shows two overlapping distributions, one peaking near 0.0 and another slightly above 0.0. The plot contains two groups: IBD and No IBD. IBD points are represented by circular markers and No IBD points by circular markers. The p PER&#132;M&#132;A&#132;N&#132;OVA value is 0.854.)
