/A 2100 0 R
/Alt (The two panel graph shows phylum level taxonomic composition. Panel a is a stacked bar graph with a vertical axis labelled Relative abundance percentage from 0 to 100 and a horizontal axis with two categories, IBD and No IBD. The bar for IBD and No IBD both show Firmicutes as the most abundant phylum, followed by Bacteroidetes. Panel b is a box plot with a vertical axis labelled Relative abundance percentage from 0 to 80 and a horizontal axis listing 10 phyla. For each phylum, two box plots compare IBD and No IBD groups. Firmicutes shows the highest relative abundance for both groups, with IBD having a slightly higher median. Bacteroidetes is the second most abundant, with No IBD showing a slightly higher median. Other phyla show decreasing abundance.)
