/Alt (The four-panel graph arranged in a two-by-two grid shows taxonomic profiling. Panel a is a stacked bar graph displaying relative abundance percentage on the vertical axis from 0 to 100. The horizontal axis shows IBD and No IBD groups. Each bar is segmented by genus, with Streptococcus, Rothia, Prevotella 7, Veillonella, Haemophilus, Gemella, Actinomyces, Fusobacterium, Neisseria, Prevotella, Granulicatella, Alloprevotella, Leptotrichia, Porphyromonas, Corynebacterium 1, and Others listed in the legend. Panel b is a box plot showing relative abundance percentage on the vertical axis from 0 to 80. The horizontal axis lists 15 genera. For each genus, two box plots compare IBD and No IBD groups. Panel c is a heatmap visualising genus abundance. The vertical axis lists 30 genera. The horizontal axis shows samples, clustered into IBD and No IBD groups. A scale bar indicates relative abundance from 0.01 to 10.00. Panel d is a two-set Venn diagram. The left circle represents IBD, the right circle represents No IBD. The IBD circle shows 59 genera with 0 percentage. The intersection shows 201 genera with 99.9 percentage. The No IBD circle shows 64 genera with 0.1 percentage.)
