/A 2115 0 R
/Alt (The two panel graph shows microbial abundance. Panel a is a volcano plot with a horizontal axis labelled Log fold change No IBD versus IBD ranging from minus 1.0 to 1.5 and a vertical axis labelled minus log10 P ranging from 0 to 4. A vertical dashed line is at 0.0 on the horizontal axis. Several points are plotted, with some labelled. Labelled points include Unclassified o Burkholderiales at approximately minus 1.0, Cloacibacterium at minus 0.8, Curvibacter at minus 0.7, Shuttleworthia at 0.7, Yersinia at 1.3, Faecalibacterium at 0.8, Gardnerella at 0.7, and Unclassified f Comamonadace at 0.9. Panel b is a horizontal bar graph with a horizontal axis labelled Relative abundance percentage ranging from 0.00 to 0.15. The vertical axis lists genera: Anaeroglobus, Yersinia, Cloacibacterium, Shuttleworthia, Curvibacter, Faecalibacterium, and Gardnerella. A legend indicates IBD is represented by a light purple bar and No IBD by a light teal bar. For Anaeroglobus, No IBD is higher than IBD. For Yersinia, No IBD is higher than IBD. For Cloacibacterium, IBD is higher than No IBD. For Shuttleworthia, IBD is higher than No IBD. For Curvibacter, IBD is higher than No IBD. For Faecalibacterium, IBD is higher than No IBD. For Gardnerella, IBD is higher than No IBD. Error bars are present for all bars.)
