/A 2119 0 R
/Alt (The two-panel figure shows a horizontal bar graph in panel a and six paired bar graphs in panel b. Panel a, titled Mean Decrease Gini, displays a horizontal bar graph with six bacterial genera listed on the vertical axis: Porphyromonas, Fusobacterium, Dialister, Catonella, Anaeroglobus, and Micrococcus. The horizontal axis ranges from 0.0 to 10.0. Porphyromonas has the longest bar, extending to approximately 9.0, marked with two asterisks. Fusobacterium extends to approximately 6.5, Dialister to approximately 6.0, Catonella to approximately 5.0, and Anaeroglobus to approximately 4.5, each marked with one asterisk. Micrococcus has the shortest bar, extending to approximately 1.0, marked with one asterisk. Panel b contains six paired bar graphs, each showing Relative abundance percentage on the vertical axis for IBD and No IBD groups. The graphs are for Anaeroglobus, Catonella, Dialister, Fusobacterium, Micrococcus, and Porphyromonas. For Anaeroglobus, the No IBD bar is higher than the IBD bar. For Catonella, the No IBD bar is higher than the IBD bar. For Dialister, the No IBD bar is higher than the IBD bar. For Fusobacterium, the No IBD bar is higher than the IBD bar. For Micrococcus, the IBD bar is higher than the No IBD bar. For Porphyromonas, the No IBD bar is higher than the IBD bar.)
/K 7
/P 36 0 R
/Pg 24 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
