/A 2123 0 R
/Alt (The two panel figure shows bar graphs comparing bacterial genera. Panel a displays a horizontal bar graph with LDA score on the horizontal axis ranging from minus 2 to 2. The vertical axis lists six bacterial genera: g Micrococcus, g Catonella, g Anaeroglobus, g Dialister, g Porphyromonas, and g Fusobacterium. g Micrococcus has a positive LDA score of approximately 1.5. All other genera have negative LDA scores, with g Catonella at approximately minus 1.5, g Anaeroglobus at minus 2, g Dialister at minus 1.8, g Porphyromonas at minus 2, and g Fusobacterium at minus 2. Panel b displays a horizontal paired bar graph with relative abundance on the horizontal axis ranging from 0.00 to 0.04. The vertical axis lists the same six bacterial genera. Each genus has two horizontal bars, one for IBD and one for No IBD, with error bars. For g Micrococcus, the IBD group has a higher relative abundance than the No IBD group. For g Catonella, g Anaeroglobus, g Dialister, g Porphyromonas, and g Fusobacterium, the No IBD group consistently shows a higher relative abundance than the IBD group. An inset in panel b shows a magnified view for g Micrococcus and g Catonella, with relative abundance ranging from 0.00000 to 0.00100, confirming the same trends.)
