/Alt (The two-panel network diagram shows microbial association networks. Panel a, labelled IBD, displays a network with nodes representing genera and edges representing SparCC correlations. Node sizes vary, and edges are solid for positive correlations or dashed for negative correlations, with thickness proportional to correlation magnitude. Several nodes are circled in red, indicating hub taxa, including g Capnocytophaga, UC o Bacteroidales, and g Haemophilus. Panel b, labelled No IBD, shows a similar network, but with a higher density of nodes and connections. Hub taxa in panel b include g Prevotella, g Megasphaera, and g Veillonella. A legend to the right defines node colours by phylum: Proteobacteria, Fusobacteria, Synergistetes, Cyanobacteria, Actinobacteria, Candidate division SR1, Saccharibacteria, Bacteroidetes, Tenericutes, Firmicutes, and Spirochaetae. The legend also indicates dashed lines for negative correlation, solid lines for positive correlation, and a red circle for hub taxa.)
/K 4
/P 36 0 R
/Pg 25 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
