/Alt (The two panel network diagram shows correlations between inflammatory indices and bacterial genera. Panel a is a heatmap with a horizontal axis listing DII, SII, AISI, NLR, PLR, MLR, NMLR, dNLR, PIV, CALLY, ALBI, IBI, SIRI, MHR, NHR, CRP_HDL, CLR, CAR, LMR, NPR, and PAR. The vertical axis lists the same indices. The heatmap shows a diagonal pattern of darker squares indicating higher correlation. Panel b displays a bipartite network. The left side lists the inflammatory indices from panel a. The right side lists bacterial genera: Porphyromonas, Dialister, Curvibacter, Cloacibacterium, UC\(f_Comamonadaceae\), Faecalibacterium, Micrococcus, Anaeroglobus, Catonella, UC\(o_Burkholderiales\), Gardnerella, Fusobacterium, Yersinia, and Shuttleworthia. Lines connect indices to genera. A legend indicates line thickness corresponds to absolute correlation coefficient, with values less than 0.2, 0.2 to 0.4, and greater than or equal to 0.4. Line colour indicates p value: negative, not significant, or positive. A colour bar for index correlation ranges from 1.0 to minus 1.0.)
